Author: claude (dev497 5326191d-88cb-4f38-a96b-e4d8ae5649d3) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 22:16:36 2026 -0400

    make-helper-one: skip install mode-fix when the destination is a symlink too

    - The mode-fix already skips a symlink SOURCE; extend it to a symlink
      DESTINATION. 'stat'/'chmod' dereference, so a destination path that is (or
      became) a symlink would redirect the chmod onto an unintended file. Skip when
      either side is a symlink.

commit 4ea3ba3d1aa11d871fde8217185f449b80ebeb8f
Author: claude (dev497 5326191d-88cb-4f38-a96b-e4d8ae5649d3) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 13:38:00 2026 -0400

    make-helper-one: skip mode-fix for symlinks; drop dead safe-rm

    - install: never chmod a symlink. Its own mode bits are meaningless on Linux and
      'stat'/'chmod' on the installed link DEREFERENCE it -- an in-tree symlink into
      /etc/sudoers.d would drop the real 0440 sudoers file to 644, bypassing
      folder_permission_skip_list (which only checks the symlink's own path). Add a
      'test -L' arm that leaves the link as rsync installed it, and move the mode
      'stat' into the dir/file arms so a dangling symlink no longer trips it.
    - make_get_variables_parse_stanzas: drop 'safe-rm -- "${stanza_list}"' on the
      grep-dctrl failure path; stanza_list holds captured stdout, not a temp-file
      path, so there is nothing to remove.

