Author: claude (dev497 5326191d-88cb-4f38-a96b-e4d8ae5649d3) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 08:15:15 2026 -0400

    make-helper-one: nounset-safe SUDO_TO_ROOT; installcheck reads root-only files via sudo

    - make_init: '[ -n "${SUDO_TO_ROOT}" ]' tripped 'set -o nounset' with
      'SUDO_TO_ROOT: unbound variable' when genmkfile runs standalone. Guard with
      '${SUDO_TO_ROOT:-}'.
    - make_installcheck: a root-owned installed config (e.g. /etc/sudoers.d, 0440)
      is unreadable to a non-root check, so a bare 'diff' failed "Permission denied"
      and misreported it as changed. Read it via sudo for the diff; if sudo cannot,
      emit an honest not-readable notice and skip. No false change, no hard abort.
    - Silence SC2086 on the existing make_deb_install apt-get SUDO_TO_ROOT prefix.

