Date:   Mon Sep 7 23:31:48 2026 -0400

    Flush the last debian/control stanza; tighten pkg-name guard

    - make_get_variables_parse_stanzas flushes a stanza only on a following blank
      line, but "$(grep-dctrl ...)" strips grep-dctrl's trailing blank, so the LAST
      stanza was never flushed: a single-binary package (e.g. developer-meta-files)
      got an EMPTY make_package_debs_files_list, so deb-install installed nothing and
      installcheck then failed on a shipped-but-absent file. Re-add a terminator.
    - The package-name guard accepted a bare '..' (regex '^[-a-z0-9+.]+$'); anchor the
      first character to an alphanumeric per Debian policy so a name that feeds a
      deletion path cannot be '..'/'.'-prefixed.

