commit 4169ec02bc220f61772ed024cc48f46518df3b88
Author: claude (dev398 81507c04-79a4-4eef-9538-c396044dcb7b) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 2 03:13:21 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: force dpkg-architecture to honor the target arch (-f)

    dpkg-architecture ignores -a when DEB_HOST_ARCH is already set in the env
    (a cross-build, or after 'eval $(dpkg-architecture -s)'), so the wildcard
    match read the ENV arch not ${target} -- dropping a covered .deb or
    inventing one dpkg-buildpackage never builds. Add -f.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit bdf673cad541d0f1c3a153d370041c7291e8b36a
Author: claude (dev398 81507c04-79a4-4eef-9538-c396044dcb7b) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 2 02:17:37 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: fix ai-review findings (control parse + dispatch guards)

    - parse_control_package_stanzas: capture grep-dctrl with an explicit rc
      check; a malformed control silently dropped the remaining binary
      packages via a process-sub that swallowed grep-dctrl's non-zero exit.
    - rename it off the make_* namespace so make_parse_cmd cannot dispatch it
      as a bogus CLI target (it would double-append the build arrays).
    - make_debinstfile_create: enforce the debian/install + nogenmkfile
      overwrite guards HERE, so a direct 'debinstfile-create' cannot bypass
      them and clobber a hand-maintained install file.
    - make_architecture_covers_target: match via 'dpkg-architecture -i' so an
      'any-<cpu>' wildcard (e.g. any-arm covering armhf) is not dropped.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 873dd79eaf0068aecb5cbdbe1bb212fff81d6fbe
Author: claude (dev398 81507c04-79a4-4eef-9538-c396044dcb7b) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 2 00:07:18 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: keep the LOCAL tracking-ref push-skip (zero round-trip)

    Reverts the ls-remote / just-push detour. The point of the skip is ZERO
    network calls when up to date: a many-repo push loop (e.g.
    dm-packaging-helper-script) must not open a connection per remote just to
    learn there is nothing to push, or it risks a rate-limit ban. The stale
    tracking ref after a url-repoint is an accepted tradeoff, now documented
    so it is not "fixed" with ls-remote again.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 885f6a019633043fa9c5174308395b1c51336648
Author: claude (dev398 81507c04-79a4-4eef-9538-c396044dcb7b) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 1 23:56:58 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: push branches unconditionally (dm model), no tip pre-check

    git push already no-ops cheaply when a remote is current, so the branch
    tip pre-check was pure downside: a local tracking ref went stale
    (url-repoint / peer push) and skipped a needed push; an ls-remote
    pre-check adds a round-trip before the push. Match dm-packaging-helper
    -script's unsigned push -- just push. Immutable tags stay locally cached.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 4527418de3bf61cbfa3ec5727e5de0da81fba008
Author: claude (dev398 81507c04-79a4-4eef-9538-c396044dcb7b) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 1 23:42:54 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: match the remote branch ref exactly in push-skip

    ls-remote refspec patterns tail-match, so a decoy ref ending in
    /refs/heads/<branch> (e.g. a filter-branch refs/original leftover) also
    returns; NR==1 could read the decoy's sha and re-skip a needed push.
    Match field 2 == refs/heads/<branch>.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

