commit 00933bbed9f3b1944d5023b6de7a6aff5dc6ff34
Author: claude (dev270 e3958e5b-3597-4724-96f6-6207667e9d6f) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 21 01:38:57 2026 -0400

    make-helper-one: fix secondary-architecture build selection

    The per-architecture binary loop (make_cross_build_platform_list with more
    than one entry) skipped exactly the wrong builds.

    all_package_debs_are_arch_all is 'true' only when EVERY binary a package
    emits is 'Architecture: all'. The secondary-architecture skip must fire in
    that case (the arch-all .debs were already produced while targeting the
    first architecture), but it fired on 'false' -- so a package carrying an
    'Architecture: any' binary was never built for any non-first architecture,
    while a pure arch-all package was needlessly rebuilt under emulation.

    - Invert the skip condition to 'true'.
    - An excluded 'Architecture:' stanza produces no artifact for this target;
      stop clearing the flag for it, so it no longer forces a pointless
      secondary build.
    - The secondary-build cleanup 'safe-rm -- .../*_all.deb' ran with nullglob
      unset. A pure 'Architecture: any' package produces no '*_all.deb', so the
      unmatched glob passed the literal pattern to safe-rm and aborted the build
      under errexit. Collect real matches only. Newly reachable once the skip is
      fixed.

    Regression coverage: dist-ai genmkfile-tests/secondary_arch_build_test.sh.
    Reported by CodeRabbit on org-ai-assisted/genmkfile PR #42.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

