Author: claude (dev206 b8d95043-6ec9-453b-b74e-00ba3a46cfdc) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 13 05:10:56 2026 -0400

    make_strip_build_residue: depth-floor the sweep, take stray .pyc/.pyo

    The recursive residue sweep matched "${PWD}" itself, so a package root that
    happens to be named __pycache__ (or .pytest_cache, ...) was handed to
    safe-rm -r and wiped -- the debian/ guard does not exclude that case. Add
    -mindepth 1 so the root is never a match.

