commit dd257907df9a165a5d88880e9e9186f66c1274fe
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 12:57:33 2026 -0400

    install: match the permission skip-list on path boundaries, not as a substring

    - folder_permission_skip_list decides which files keep the mode they arrived
      with. The lookup used array_match, a SUBSTRING test, so an entry of '/usr/src'
      also matched '/usr/share/doc/x/usr/src-notes' and that file silently kept
      whatever mode it had -- the quiet wrong-permission outcome again.
    - Reproduced against the shipped function before fixing.
    - path_is_within_any matches the path itself or the '/' boundary beneath it, so
      '/usr/src/foo' still matches and '/usr/share/doc/x/usr/src-notes' no longer
      does.
    - array_match itself is untouched: it is generic, has no other caller here, and
      a package's make-helper-overrides.bsh is sourced into this shell and may use
      it.
    - Covered in dist-ai genmkfile-tests/install_modes_test.sh: a file genuinely
      under a skipped folder keeps mode 0600, one merely containing the text is
      fixed to 0644. The second assertion fails on the substring predicate.

commit a8c0fd08fbf36caa1947646dcb769e293bcf7419
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 12:54:17 2026 -0400

    uninstall: see dangling symlinks, so a leftover cannot report as a clean uninstall

    - 'test -f' follows the link, so it is FALSE for a symlink whose target is gone.
      uninstall therefore skipped such a file AND uninstallcheck then exited 0
      reporting a clean uninstall with the file still on disk. Neither step said
      anything: a false green on both.
    - Reproduced before fixing: a relative in-tree symlink with a missing target is
      installed by rsync --safe-links (it does not escape the tree), survives
      'uninstall', and 'uninstallcheck' exits 0.
    - genmkfile_path_present is file-or-symlink, NOT '-e': '-e' is also true for a
      DIRECTORY, and the loop hands each hit to safe-rm, which then fails with
      "Is a directory". Excluding directories is the part the old '-f' had right.
      Verified -- that wrong turn aborts uninstall outright.
    - Applied to uninstall, uninstallsim and uninstallcheck, which shared the
      predicate.
    - Covered by dist-ai genmkfile-tests/uninstall_completeness_test.sh (8 checks),
      which asserts both halves. It fails on the old predicate ("left the dangling
      symlink behind") and on the too-broad one ("Is a directory").

commit 74227f6e49da1fcdbc28d8895b36840ccdbcae95
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 12:10:52 2026 -0400

    deb-cleanup: sweep artifacts that carry no Debian revision

    - Every glob in the table required a literal '-', so two real shapes were never
      matched:
        <pkg>_1.0.orig.tar.xz   the upstream tarball is named from make_pkg_version
                                WITHOUT the revision, so it never has a hyphen
        <pkg>_2.0_all.deb       a version with no Debian revision
      Verified against real artifacts, not hypothesised.
    - Effect: every PREVIOUS version's orig tarball accumulated in DISTDIR forever.
      The CURRENT one was removed by the exact-path fallback at the end of the
      function, which is exactly what hid the defect. A revision-less .deb was never
      swept at all, leaving a stale binary for a later build to publish or install.
      DISTDIR is the .deb cache deb-pkg and reprepro read from.
    - The leading '<pkg>_' still anchors each pattern, so a sibling package is
      untouched: '<pkg>-extra_1.0-1_all.deb' does not match '<pkg>_'*.
    - Covered by dist-ai genmkfile-tests/deb_cleanup_artifacts_test.sh: a seeded
      DISTDIR asserting 11 artifacts are swept AND 4 belonging to other packages
      survive. 2 assertions fail on the old table; over-deletion would fail the
      other 4.
    - Verified: full genmkfile suite green, and a real cowbuilder deb-pkg build
      still produces exactly the expected artifact set.

commit 329e2443119b761438707ba8c175d5c58744d39d
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
