commit ca1e28b57be9bcd980030a514bf10e27efc4092a
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 11:31:42 2026 -0400

    version parsing: take the revision from the LAST hyphen, and strip it before arithmetic

    Both found by CodeRabbit review on the PR; both verified against the code and
    reproduced before fixing.

    - Debian permits hyphens in the upstream version and defines the revision as the
      part after the LAST hyphen. The revision was taken from the FIRST hyphen while
      the version stripped at the last one, so the halves disagreed: '1.0-beta-1'
      gave version '1.0-beta' and revision '-beta-1', and every derived name came
      out '1.0-beta-beta-1' (.dsc, .orig.tar.xz, .debian.tar.xz, .changes, each
      .deb). Ordinary '0.1-1' and epoch forms are unaffected.
    - make_pkg_revision carries its leading hyphen on purpose, because callers
      concatenate it straight into artifact names. The major-bump path fed it to bc
      as-is, so 'scale=9 ; -1 + 1' returned 0 and a bump of '1.0-1' produced '1.0-0'
      -- a downgrade debchange rejects. Stripped before the arithmetic; an empty
      revision now bumps to 1 rather than being a syntax error.
    - The split moves into make_parse_changelog_version so it can be exercised
      directly. No behaviour change from the extraction itself.
    - genmkfile-tests/test_version_parse.sh: 12 checks over the shapes named in
      make_get_variables' own comment plus the hyphenated ones, including a
      round-trip that rebuilds the input the way callers do. 4 fail on the old
      split, naming '1.0-beta-1 -> 1.0-beta-beta-1'.
    - Verified: gate green, both genmkfile test suites green, and a real cowbuilder
      deb-pkg build still produces private-ai-config_0.1-1_all.deb.

commit 944fc03b98e8ba7d6af0df90d08f72682d946e0f
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 11:17:18 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: finish the SC2250 / R-010 sweep across the remaining shell files

    - make-helper.bsh and shared.bsh were the last two files still carrying SC2250
      (25 and 3). Braced by shellcheck's own '--format=diff' auto-fix, not by hand.
    - make-helper.bsh: completes the strict-mode block with 'shopt -s shift_verbose'
      and anchors 'source=SCRIPTDIR/shared.bsh' to './shared.bsh' (R-080). The file
      contains no 'shift', so shift_verbose changes nothing at runtime.
    - shared.bsh: takes the documented no-strict exemption instead of a strict
      block. It is sourced-only, so setting errexit / nounset / pipefail there would
      leak them into the sourcing shell -- the same reason make-helper-one.bsh
      carries that marker.
    - The whole repo now passes the gate, so a future one-line change is no longer
      blocked by inherited debt in whatever file it touches.
    - Verified: bash -n clean, 0 SC2250 repo-wide, genmkfile's own test suite green,
      and a real cowbuilder 'deb-pkg' build of an unrelated package exits 0.

commit 6a702df446579ce5d2ebf49899d1a65e8519b44f
Author: claude (dev163 38f9745c-aed1-4fb4-b6ae-9899f20f8de2) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 10:54:40 2026 -0400

    deb-cleanup: only strip residue in a package source root

    - The rest of this file also assumes PWD is the package root, but those
      functions delete a handful of specifically named artifacts. This one deletes
