commit 0dc4188d185f221c4e0841e6584f6ca47bb6075f
Author: claude (dev163 38f9745c-aed1-4fb4-b6ae-9899f20f8de2) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 10:20:18 2026 -0400

    deb-cleanup: strip python build residue before packaging

    - Packaging copies the WORKING TREE, not git's view, so a .mypy_cache or
      __pycache__ left in the source tree by in-tree linting is shipped inside the
      .deb even though it is already in .gitignore. lintian then fails the build
      closed on package-contains-python-dot-directory.
    - Strip .mypy_cache, __pycache__ and .hypothesis in make_deb_cleanup, which
      runs before the tree is packaged.
    - '.git' is pruned so a residue-named directory inside it cannot be deleted.
    - '-prune' on a match stops find descending into a directory it is about to
      delete, so nested residue cannot produce stale entries.
    - Removed paths are printed: a silent sweep in a build tool is
      indistinguishable from one that removed the wrong thing.
    - find runs in the foreground rather than through 'while read < <(find ...)':
      process substitution hides find's exit status, so under errexit a broken
      find would strip nothing while the build continued looking clean.

    Test asserts BOTH directions -- residue removed, and real sources, a
    similarly-named directory and .git contents left alone. Canaried: gutting the
    removal fails exactly the three residue cases; dropping the .git prune fails
    exactly the .git case.

    ## AI-Assisted

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 98ee6efe86c624ef357eaaf36df73d46098914d4
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 10:13:20 2026 -0400

    cowbuilder: clear the inherited temp-dir vars so libpam-tmpdir stops breaking builds

    - libpam-tmpdir sets TMPDIR=/tmp/user/0 for sudo's root session. pbuilder passes
      it into the chroot, where that path does not exist, and the build dies with
      "dpkg-deb: error: failed to make temporary file (control member)" during
      pbuilder-satisfydepends. Debian #823651.
    - Enables the --unset block that was already written here and commented out,
      placed after sudo: sudo's env_reset discards anything set on the calling side,
      so the same assignment earlier would silently do nothing.
    - Callers no longer need a per-machine --configfile purely to work around this.
      Verified: 'genmkfile deb-pkg' with make_use_cowbuilder=true and NO --configfile
      builds green on a libpam-tmpdir host; without the fix the same invocation fails
      with the dpkg-deb error above.
    - A private per-build temp dir is not an option and the comment now says so:
      TMPDIR crosses into the chroot, so a host-side mktemp path does not exist
      there. Measured -- it reproduces the identical dpkg-deb failure.

commit 63cb85096d7bccb9fa103aef5fc90720ad6dc8d1
Author: claude (dev166 9381e85d-1ecd-45ca-9b11-d43120f634e1) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 10:12:44 2026 -0400

    make-helper-one: brace variable references (SC2250) and anchor the source directive

    - Mechanical only, no behaviour change. Separated from the fix that follows so
      that one stays reviewable.
    - Generated by shellcheck's own '--format=diff' auto-fix, not by hand, so the
      substitutions are exactly what the checker asks for: 322 lines.
    - R-080: 'source=SCRIPTDIR/shared.bsh' -> './shared.bsh'; the directive must be
      relative and anchored.
    - Verified: bash -n clean, shellcheck reports 0 SC2250, and a real
      'genmkfile deb-pkg' cowbuilder build of an unrelated package still exits 0.

commit 27ef52a4ba78e38b654068a8b96c4707767fc5c8
Author: claude (dev163 38f9745c-aed1-4fb4-b6ae-9899f20f8de2) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 7 22:28:14 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: diagnostics to stderr

    The makefile-full failure block wrote its error text, the 'ls -la' listing and
    the chmod remediation to STDOUT. genmkfile's stdout is consumed by callers, so a
    make wrapper reading it received the diagnostics as if they were data.

    The detection-failure branch above already used '>&2'; this block did not.

    Found by coderabbit.

    Testing
    -------

    Gate exit 0 in an ISOLATED checkout.

      4 pass, 0 fail

      GENMKFILE_PATH unset, ./usr/share found   same
      GENMKFILE_PATH set explicitly             same
      makefile-full present but UNREADABLE      differ
      GENMKFILE_PATH directory unlistable (000) differ

    The last two are asserted to DIFFER: they are the cases that run the block, so
    moving it between streams must be visible there and nowhere else.

    Canary: removing the eight redirects gives 2 pass / 2 fail, failing exactly
    those two.

    Two harness changes were needed to see this at all:
    - stdout and stderr are captured SEPARATELY now. Merged with '2>&1' a diagnostic
      moving from one stream to the other is invisible -- the harness reported
      '4 same, 0 differing' for a change that moved every line in the block.
    - '$?' is read immediately after the command. Appending the stderr capture first
      made 'status' the exit code of that assignment rather than of genmkfile.

    And the fixture had gone stale: the earlier refresh was short-circuited by a
    failing shellcheck in the same '&&' chain, so the run compared against the
    previous build. refresh-fixture.sh exists for exactly this and has to actually
    run.

commit 5e90e7f664b013cfb75de24447f52aebb5f919cc
Author: claude (dev163 38f9745c-aed1-4fb4-b6ae-9899f20f8de2) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 7 13:54:34 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: keep the permission diagnostic best-effort under errexit

    The makefile-full-unreadable branch runs 'ls -la' as a debugging aid, then
    prints the chmod remediation, then falls through to make-helper.bsh -- it warns,
    it does not stop.

    Under the errexit added in the previous commit, a GENMKFILE_PATH directory the
    caller cannot list makes that 'ls' fail and aborts the script right there. The
    chmod remediation -- the one output that actually helps -- is swallowed, and the
    make-helper.bsh attempt this branch deliberately still makes never happens. The
    very permission problem the diagnostic exists to show is what kills it.

    '|| true' on the ls, with the reason in a comment.

    Testing
    -------

    The earlier harness did NOT catch this: its 'unreadable' case chmod 0000's
    makefile-full but leaves the DIRECTORY listable, so the 'ls' succeeds and the
    abort never fires. A case for the unlistable directory is added.

      4 same, 0 differing

    Canary: removing the '|| true' gives 3 same, 1 differing, and only the new case
    moves -- old exit 126 (master reached make-helper.bsh and was denied), new exit
    2 (aborted at the ls).

    Found by codex and agy independently.

    Gate exit 0 in an isolated checkout.

commit 855235ea235121b1f0941c6a3e254a6cb64daad1
Author: claude (dev163 38f9745c-aed1-4fb4-b6ae-9899f20f8de2) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 7 13:44:00 2026 -0400

    genmkfile: R-010 strict mode

    usr/bin/genmkfile locates GENMKFILE_PATH -- from the environment, or by probing
    three candidate directories -- and hands off to make-helper.bsh.

    Real nounset trap
    -----------------

    GENMKFILE_PATH is read by 'if [ "$GENMKFILE_PATH" = "" ]', the test whose whole
    job is to detect it being unset. Under nounset that aborted before the probing
    could run at all, so genmkfile would not work unless the caller had already
    exported the variable it exists to derive.

    The detection-failure branch now stops
    ----------------------------------------

    It printed "Auto detection of GENMKFILE_PATH failed!" and CARRIED ON: into
    'realpath ""', then a makefile-full check against an empty path, then
    make-helper.bsh invoked with nothing -- a cascade of follow-on errors after the
    real one had already been reported. It now exits 1 there, and the message goes
    to stderr.

    Also 7 'echo' -> printf (R-034) and '--' before the realpath, ls, cd, dirname
    and pushd operands.

    Testing
    -------

    Gate exit 0 in an ISOLATED checkout.

      3 same, 0 differing

    Three cases: GENMKFILE_PATH unset with a discoverable share directory,
    GENMKFILE_PATH set explicitly, and makefile-full present but UNREADABLE.

    Canary: removing the '${GENMKFILE_PATH:-}' default gives 1 same, 2 differing --
    both unset cases abort.

    NOT COVERED, and worth saying so: the detection-FAILURE path. Removing the
    fixture's share directory does not make detection fail, because the third
    candidate is the absolute '/usr/share/genmkfile', which exists on any machine
    with genmkfile installed -- including the test host. A case built that way
    silently exercises the SYSTEM installation instead of the fixture, and the two
    variants then differ for reasons unrelated to the change. Covering it needs the
    system path hidden:
      bwrap --dev-bind / / --tmpfs /usr/share/genmkfile -- <the script>
    The harness says this in a comment where the case would otherwise have gone.

