commit 012520fc0280986cad130457a5467960dbf7b437
Author: claude (dev113 6465e658-44ed-4e80-93cf-c9586d8683d6) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 28 11:48:34 2026 -0400

    distclean: also drop debhelper residue

    'genmkfile distclean' ran only the Makefile's clean target, so it left
    debian/.debhelper, debian/files, debian/debhelper-build-stamp, the per-package
    staging dir and *.substvars behind. 'genmkfile dist' then refuses the tree with
    "Empty directory found!", i.e. distclean could not restore a tree that dist
    accepts. Run make_deb_clean as well.

    Verified in a disposable VM against this package's own source:
    - in-place build leaves .debhelper / genmkfile / files / debhelper-build-stamp
      / genmkfile.substvars
    - BEFORE: distclean cleared none of them, and 'genmkfile dist' failed with
      "Empty directory found!"
    - AFTER: distclean cleared all of them and 'genmkfile dist' succeeded
    - 'distclean' and 'deb-cleanup' both still exit 0

    deb-cleanup keeps its wider scope (debian/rules clean plus the debuild artifacts
    in the parent folder); this only makes distclean self-consistent with dist.

    Generated with assistance from Claude Code.

