    skill: cowbuilder is mandatory; drop the in-place build path

    - Packages are ALWAYS built in a cowbuilder chroot. An in-place build ties the
      .deb to host state instead of a declared chroot and leaves debhelper residue
      that later fails the pristine-tree check.
    - A missing cowbuilder base means recreate the base, not fall back in-place.
    - Enforced by the cowbuilder-guard PreToolUse hook; COWBUILDER_GUARD_ALLOW=1 is
      the deliberate override.

