commit c8f82892fd4bf60d757b696f36a4903087e3196a
Author: claude (dev74 3cdbae8e-30ec-412d-8ce2-ba63d1c9b6af) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 23 11:00:37 2026 -0400

    reprepro include: accept arch-all build-host buildinfo (--ignore=surprisingarch)

    An Architecture:all package (e.g. developer-meta-files) ships a build-host
    buildinfo named '<pkg>_<build-arch>.buildinfo' (amd64), whose architecture is
    not listed in the .changes 'Architecture: all source' header. A distribution
    configured with 'Tracking: minimal includebuildinfos ...' makes reprepro process
    that buildinfo and reject the include as 'surprisingarch', aborting the upload:

      '..._amd64.buildinfo' looks like architecture 'amd64', but this is not listed
      in the Architecture-Header!  To ignore use --ignore=surprisingarch.

    The aptrepo_local distribution has no Tracking line, so it never includes the
    buildinfo and succeeds; only tracking-enabled (aptrepo_remote) distributions hit
    this. Pass --ignore=surprisingarch alongside the existing --ignore=wrongdistribution
    on the include; this is the standard handling for arch-all build metadata and does
    not affect arch-specific packages.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

