    deb-pkg: allow a per-build cow snapshot suffix (make_cow_suffix)

    Append an optional '$make_cow_suffix' to the writable cowbuilder snapshot path
    (cow.cow_<arch><suffix>) so a caller can run several 'deb-pkg' builds concurrently,
    each with its own snapshot, without colliding on one 'cow.cow_<arch>'. Empty by
    default -> unchanged single-build behavior. The read-only 'base.cow_<arch>' stays
    shared (cowbuilder only reads it to seed each snapshot). Enables package-level
    parallelism in derivative-maker's 2100_create-debian-packages.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

