commit f1d0d57387c8c0499c99b8d3471c919f79709434
Author: claude (dev74 3cdbae8e-30ec-412d-8ce2-ba63d1c9b6af) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 13 10:39:25 2026 -0400

    make-helper-one: run cowbuilder builds under UNSHARE_PID_NS when set

    Run the cowbuilder .deb build as the init of a private PID namespace so
    nothing started inside the chroot session can outlive the build; when
    cowbuilder exits, the kernel SIGKILLs every process left in the
    namespace (upstream pbuilder deliberately has no process reaper).

    The wrapper is the UNSHARE_PID_NS variable set and exported by
    derivative-maker help-steps/pre (the single source of truth, typically
    'unshare --pid --fork --kill-child --'). When genmkfile runs standalone
    the variable is unset and '${UNSHARE_PID_NS:-}' expands to nothing, so
    unprivileged standalone builds keep working unchanged.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

