commit 2d84780f900f48d14f383b4a78be9f6a6070f627
Author: claude (dev22 c20093f1-1b30-4397-87b6-9586321c87df) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 1 04:08:52 2026 -0400

    make_get_variables: keep arch-excluded binary in make_package_list

    Follow-up to the arch-restricted .deb skip: the previous change used
    'continue', which also dropped the excluded binary from make_package_list,
    not just from make_package_debs_files_list. make_package_list is iterated by
    reprepro remove/removesrc (make_reprepro_shared) and by deb-cleanup, so an
    arch-excluded package (e.g. firmware-nonfreedom on arm64) would no longer be
    cleaned up / removed there.

    Skip only the expected-artifact append (make_package_debs_files_list) via a
    skip_debs_artifact flag, and still add the package to make_package_list.
    reprepro-add uses the .changes file (not make_package_list), so keeping it
    there does not cause an add of a non-existent .deb; and reprepro
    remove/removesrc of an absent package is a no-op (exit 0, verified), so
    cleanup/removal stays safe.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018bezwAzE9uxSX1xrH7okFV

commit d07583e5ad92c922593887731603c63f03c7c6f4
Author: claude (dev22 c20093f1-1b30-4397-87b6-9586321c87df) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 1 01:17:42 2026 -0400

    make_get_variables: skip binary stanzas whose Architecture excludes target

    When computing make_package_debs_files_list (the .deb artifacts each binary
    stanza is expected to produce), an 'Architecture:' field that is neither
    'all' nor covers the current build (target) architecture means
    dpkg-buildpackage emits no .deb for that stanza -- so it must not be listed
    as an expected artifact.

    Previously the expected .deb filename was derived from the literal
    'Architecture:' field, so e.g. 'Architecture: amd64' produced an expected
    '<pkg>_<ver>_amd64.deb' even on an arm64 build. dpkg-buildpackage building
    for arm64 does not build that stanza, so the existence check in
    make_deb_pkg_build_shared died with "File '..._amd64.deb' does not exist."
    This blocked arm64 (and any cross-arch) builds at kicksecure-meta-packages,
    whose 'firmware-nonfreedom' binary is 'Architecture: amd64' (it pulls
    amd64-microcode / intel-microcode).

    Add make_architecture_covers_target() to test whether an 'Architecture:'
    field value covers a target architecture (handles 'any', the 'linux-any' /
    'linux-<arch>' wildcards, and explicit space-separated lists). Use it to:
    - keep 'all' packages as-is (architecture independent, always built);
    - for architecture-dependent packages that cover the target, name the .deb
      after the target architecture (dpkg-buildpackage always does so);
    - skip packages whose Architecture excludes the target entirely.

    No change for a native build where target == the stanza's architecture
    (e.g. amd64): the computed suffix is identical, so existing amd64 builds are
    unaffected. Validated by a real arm64 kicksecure-cli build clearing the
    kicksecure-meta-packages step that previously failed here.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018bezwAzE9uxSX1xrH7okFV

