commit b2535fab6ea27135141e3f20e75e856dd911688f
Author: claude (dev22 c20093f1-1b30-4397-87b6-9586321c87df) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 30 19:20:39 2026 -0400

    SKILL: document cowbuilder --execute env-passing + cowdancer hardlink trap

    Two cowbuilder gotchas learned while removing the vbox chroot env-files:

    - 'cowbuilder --execute' forwards the caller's environment into the chroot
      script; sudo --preserve-env=<list> only carries EXPORTED variables, so a
      set-but-unexported entry is dropped. Export the vars and rely on
      --preserve-env rather than serializing a declare-p env-file to source.

    - The buildplace is a 'cp -al base' hardlink farm; cowdancer breaks a hardlink
      before a write to protect the base, but sudo's env_reset strips the cowdancer
      LD_PRELOAD/ilist, so a sudo step inside the chroot writes through hardlinks
      and corrupts the shared base. Do not reuse a base across runs after a
      non-cowdancer mutation; and run in-chroot root commands without sudo to keep
      the cowdancer env intact.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018bezwAzE9uxSX1xrH7okFV

commit 1d07352ad415a3d79234e3f3314d6a9dcc55db36
