commit 8183f3bec7b7c86aa651d6b3812ffbdde7a00f53
Author: claude (dev22 c20093f1-1b30-4397-87b6-9586321c87df) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 30 09:07:28 2026 -0400

    make_deb_install: allow opting out of installcheck via make_use_installcheck

    make_installcheck (make_helper) diffs a package's files at native FHS
    paths (bin/ etc/ usr/ ...) found in the source tree against what got
    installed -- a check that only fits genmkfile-native packages. A
    dh-packaged repo such as live-build keeps its source under share/,
    functions/, data/, frontend/ and maps it into the .deb via debian/rules,
    so there are no native-FHS files in the source tree; make_helper matches
    nothing and aborts with "Nothing has been copied" even though the .deb
    built and installed fine.

    Gate the post-install make_installcheck on make_use_installcheck (mirrors
    the existing make_use_lintian opt-out): default keeps running it, repos
    that do not fit the native model set make_use_installcheck=false in their
    overrides. Verified: 'genmkfile deb-install' on live-build now installs
    the deb and skips installcheck (exit 0) instead of dying.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018bezwAzE9uxSX1xrH7okFV

