commit 6f8a7484c9431000b6aafb335a90298c655b31fc
Author: claude (dev22 c20093f1-1b30-4397-87b6-9586321c87df) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 29 14:23:35 2026 -0400

    make_get_variables: set deb variables for git-describe repos that have debian/control

    make_use_git_describe_for_version is meant for special repos with no
    debian/control (Whonix-Installer, Whonix-Starter, qubes-template-*): they
    have no deb to build, so make_get_variables derived the git tag version
    from `git describe` and short-circuited before setting the upstream/debian
    tarball and .dsc path variables.

    live-build sets the same flag (to keep `genmkfile git-verify` working
    against its commit_<sha> tags) but DOES ship debian/control and is built
    as a .deb via `genmkfile deb-icup`. The unconditional short-circuit left
    make_upstream_tarball_relative_path et al. unset, so deb-cleanup ->
    make_undist aborted under `set -o nounset`:
      make-helper-one.bsh: make_upstream_tarball_relative_path: unbound variable

    Gate the short-circuit on the actual absence of debian/control (via
    make_debian_control_file_absolute_path, set by make_shared_function): a
    flagged repo that ships debian/control now falls through to the normal
    path and gets the deb variables, while the git-describe tag version
    computed above is preserved (the normal path's changelog-derived
    make_git_tag_version_number assignment is skipped while the flag is set),
    so git-verify still compares against the commit_<sha> tag.

    Verified: deb-cleanup on a flag+control fixture no longer trips the unbound
    variable and exits 0; git-tag-show still reports the commit_<sha> tag, not
    the changelog version; the control-less special-repo path is unchanged.
    Regression test added to the dist-ai genmkfile-tests suite.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018bezwAzE9uxSX1xrH7okFV

