    log-helpers: prefix every line with repo name; standardise format (#28)

    ## Summary

    Adds `[<repo>]` to every INFO/WARNING/ERROR/CACHED/DEBUG/running line so
    output stays greppable when many packages build in parallel.

    Before: `genmkfile: CACHED: branch 'master' (ae55be0cf5bf) already at
    remote 'origin' tip`
    After: `genmkfile: [debug-misc] CACHED: branch 'master' (ae55be0cf5bf)
    already at remote 'origin' tip`

    ## Approach

    1. Adds tiny semantic helpers (`make_info`, `make_warn`, `make_cached`,
    `make_debug`) routing through one format. `die`, `make_log_and_run`, and
    `make_require` reuse the same prefix.
    2. Resolves the repo name once at source time into
    `$_genmkfile_repo_name` (git-toplevel basename, falls back to PWD
    basename outside a git checkout). Lazy caching via a helper does not
    work because every log site invokes the helper from `$(...)` and the
    cache would die with the sub-shell.
    3. Replaces ~30 ad-hoc printf call sites; collapses 9 distinct prefix
    styles into one.
    4. Drops redundant `repo=` field from atomic-push messages.

    ## Test plan

    - [x] `bash -n` syntax check passes.
    - [x] `git_tag_push_to_remote` test harness (4 scenarios) - all still
    pass, every line carries `[<repo>]`.
    - [x] Repo-name fallback verified in a non-git directory.
    - [x] Eager-compute tested under `errexit + nounset + inherit_errexit`.


