commit a8919dc67b0cef41261c916fbcd7531dfde603c1
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed May 27 23:16:37 2026 +0000

    git-tag-push: skip 'git push' when branch tips already at remote

    Previously git_tag_push_to_remote always invoked
    'git push --atomic --porcelain -- <remote> <branch-refspecs...>'
    even when every requested tag was cache-hit and every requested
    branch was already at the remote tip. Symptom from a dm-push
    batch run on a clean tree:

      CACHED: '0.6-1' (4c10b3cb6fbd) already pushed to 'org-ai-assisted'
      running: git push --atomic --porcelain -- org-ai-assisted refs/heads/master:refs/heads/master
      ...
      To github.com:org-ai-assisted/age-api.git
      =       refs/heads/master:refs/heads/master     [up to date]

    Three TCP/SSH connections + host-key prints per repo per batch
    iteration for zero work.

    git already tracks remote branch state (refs/remotes/<remote>/<branch>),
    so there's no need to invent a parallel on-disk cache for branches the
    way tags need one. Compare local 'refs/heads/<branch>^{commit}' to the
    tracking ref; if equal, drop that branch from the push refspec list.
    If after dropping cached tags AND up-to-date branches the refspec list
    is empty, skip the 'git push' call entirely and log a CACHED line
    matching the existing tag-skip style.

    A missing tracking ref (never fetched) or one that's stale (remote
    moved forward, we haven't fetched) falls through to push -- worst
    case is the push itself reports '[up to date]', same as today.

    No behavior change when there's actually anything new to push.

