commit ab79ba86c0ee69211b626ace51aa0ced2ba426e2
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed May 27 22:23:32 2026 +0000

    make_function_run: drop rc-capture, let errexit propagate

    The wrapper previously captured the rc via

      "$function_name" "$@" || function_name_return_code="$?"
      if [ "$function_name_return_code" != "0" ]; then
         exit "$function_name_return_code"
      fi

    The '|| ...' form suspended errexit throughout the entire call subtree
    of "$function_name". Any internal command that failed and did not
    'exit' would have its rc dropped on the floor; the caller saw a
    successful return. The trip wire that surfaced this: 'genmkfile
    installcheck' running 'diff -- "$src" "$dst"' would emit
    'diff: ...: Permission denied' to stderr and still exit 0. Same risk
    class applied to rsync / chmod / safe-rm / stat inside make_helper.

    Drop the rc capture. A bare '"$function_name" "$@"' call runs under
    the script's set -o errexit (and inherit_errexit in subshells), so
    internal failures naturally surface: command fails -> errexit fires
    -> shell exits with the failing command's rc -> backgrounded
    subshells exit non-zero and parallel_wait / outer wait -n collects
    them.

    git_tag_push_to_remote's explicit 'push_rc=$?' workaround for this
    exact bug (added when atomic-push was wired up) is now redundant
    and removed in the same patch: errexit fires inside the backgrounded
    subshell on push failure, the subsequent cache-write loop never runs,
    and the subshell's non-zero exit is collected by parallel_wait.

    The one caller in the file that intercepts failure
    (make_git_commit_verify -> 'if ! sq_git_run "HEAD"; then die ...')
    already calls its target directly rather than via make_function_run,
    matching the docblock's note. No other call sites wrap
    make_function_run in '||' / '&&' / 'if !' (grep-confirmed), so
    nothing else needs adjusting.

