commit 902f068681ed668d9a499ad08cd5a0862f4d37f8
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed May 27 18:18:12 2026 +0000

    git-tag-push: parallel_wait helper, verbatim-URL cache, matched logs

    Three small cleanups on top of #23:

    1) Source helper-scripts/parallel.bsh unconditionally and replace
       the manual pids[]/pid_to_remote[]/wait loop in
       make_git_tag_push with parallel_wait + parallel_failures.
       Matches the dmf idiom; -7 lines.

    2) Cache layout simplifies from
         ${cache_dir}/<repo>/<url-hash>-<remote>.txt
           <tag>:<sha>
       to
         ${cache_dir}/<repo>/<remote>.txt
           <remote-url>:<tag>:<sha>
       Including the URL in each line still catches the 'git remote
       set-url' case (stale entries don't match the new URL, push
       proceeds) and the cache file is human-readable. Drops
       sha256sum + awk from the pipeline; drops 'sha256sum' from
       make_require too.

    3) The 'atomic push failed' die message now carries the same
       field set as the success log (branches=[], tags=[], plus the
       failed remote list in brackets) for consistent grep-ability
       in dm-push runs.

