commit 67b4c10852cbe4738de117c5011e3dadeaeafe66
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed May 27 17:44:54 2026 +0000

    git-tag-push: atomic per-remote push of branches + tip tags

    Replace the single-tag-per-call, sequential-per-remote loop with a
    unified atomic-push entry point. Every invocation bundles all
    listed branches and their tip tags into one 'git push --atomic
    --porcelain' call per remote, with remotes pushed in parallel.

    Default mode (no env vars):
      branches = current branch (errors if HEAD is detached)
      remotes  = origin
    Configured mode (env vars typically set by dm-packaging-helper-
    script):
      branches from make_git_push_branches
      remotes  from make_git_push_remotes

    Strict semantics (no fallbacks):
      - Every listed branch must exist locally, else die.
      - Every listed remote must exist locally, else die.
      - Every listed branch tip must carry a tag, else die.
    Caller is responsible for filtering env-var values to refs that
    exist in the repo.

    Skip-already-pushed cache (opt-in via make_git_tag_push_cache_dir):
      Layout: ${cache_dir}/<repo>/<url-hash>-<remote>.txt
      Lines:  <tag>:<full-40-char-commit-sha>
      url-hash catches 'git remote set-url' (stale cache for same
      remote name, different destination). Two clones with the same
      remote URL share the cache; two with different URLs do not.
      Push rc captured before cache-write loop so a failed push does
      not poison the cache. append-once + sha256sum required at
      function start (genmkfile's downstream consumers always have
      helper-scripts).

    Removed:
      - make_git_tag_push_latest (chronologically-latest-tag push;
        conflicts with the strict no-fallback rule)
      - git-tag-push-latest target in makefile-full
      - help text entry for git-tag-push-latest

    Renamed:
      - make_git_tag_push_targets -> make_git_push_remotes
        (no external callers found)

