commit dc7f7a62545f20b88175f295a0773fabf59af22e
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Mon May 18 10:29:57 2026 +0000

    make_git_tag_verify: require HEAD at the tag

    Repro: 'genmkfile git-tag-verify' in a special repo
    (make_use_git_describe_for_version) with HEAD 5 commits past a
    prior tag prints "Cached positive verification" against the
    PRIOR tag and exits 0, instead of failing as
    dm-packaging-helper-script's

        if ! genmkfile git-tag-verify; then
           dry_run_or_run genmkfile git-tag-sign
        fi

    needs it to. The downstream 'genmkfile git-verify' (which calls
    make_git_tag_check) then dies with "Current git head is a
    untagged git tag!", exposing the false-positive verify.

    Root cause: make_get_variables sets
    make_git_tag_version_number from 'git describe --abbrev=0'
    (NEAREST tag REACHABLE from HEAD, not the tag AT HEAD). The
    existing comment acknowledged this and pointed at
    make_git_tag_check as the downstream guard, but
    make_git_tag_verify went straight to 'sq_git_run
    refs/tags/$make_git_tag_version_number' without the HEAD-at-tag
    assertion, so the verify happily authenticated the prior tag.

    Fix: assert HEAD-at-tag in make_git_tag_verify using the same
    'git describe --always --abbrev=1000000000' comparison
    make_git_tag_check uses. Honour
    make_skip_git_describe_output_check (derivative-maker sets it
    in debian/make-helper-overrides.bsh) so its existing semantics
    are unchanged. Updated the stale "downstream make_git_tag_check
    still asserts ..." comment in make_get_variables.

    Verified on a synthetic special repo:
     - HEAD past tag, no override:       rc=1 (was 0), clear die msg.
     - HEAD at tag:                      rc=0, sq_git_run runs on tag.
     - HEAD past tag, override = true:   rc=0, sq_git_run runs (matches
                                         derivative-maker's pre-fix behaviour).
     - 'git-tag-check' semantics unchanged in all three cases.

