commit 985bd65cc0bd447a6e9485f6d8aae3f56b16d7d0
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Mon May 18 10:08:53 2026 +0000

    make_debinstfile_create: nounset-safe associative-array read

    Repro: 'genmkfile debinstfile' on a multi-package repo (one or
    more files in the source tree with a '#packagename' suffix) dies:

      /usr/share/genmkfile/make-helper-one.bsh: line 866:
      delete_yet[$pkg_name]: unbound variable
      cp: cannot stat '/tmp/.../tmp.XXXX/*.install': No such file or directory

    'local -A delete_yet' declares the array but does not bind any
    keys; reading '${delete_yet[$pkg_name]}' before the first write
    trips nounset (R-025 in the bash style guide: an associative
    array's *keys* are individually unbound until first assignment).
    Use the '${arr[k]:-}' default form for the read.

    The subshell-bound while-loop fails on the unbound-key read and
    exits early; the outer for-loop then sees no '*.install' files
    under '$genmkfile_temp_dir', the glob falls through to the
    literal pattern, and 'cp' reports cannot-stat. The errexit that
    should have aborted at the original failure is suppressed by the
    'make_function_run' chain (the same suppression class the prior
    PR fixed for return paths; reads-under-nounset are not affected
    by that fix because the subshell's failure is propagated via
    pipefail rather than 'return').

    Also declared 'filename_without_dot' in the 'local ...' list; it
    is set at line 860 but was previously inheriting from the calling
    scope.

