commit 5883ee627d662264fab8bd2c592d555098a150a4
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun May 17 21:37:15 2026 +0000

    make_function_run: exit on failure (don't swallow nested rcs)

    Repro: 'genmkfile git-tag-verify' on a repo where 'sq-git log'
    fails (e.g. an unsigned/missing tag) exits 0 instead of
    propagating sq-git's non-zero rc.

    Trace through the call chain when 'make_function_run X' wraps a
    function X that itself calls 'make_function_run Y':

      caller -> make_function_run X
                  "$X" "$@" || rc=$?     # || suppresses errexit in X
                  -> X
                      -> make_function_run Y
                           "$Y" "$@" || rc=$?
                           -> Y fails, rc=1
                           returns 1
                      # Y's failure ignored; X continues
                      # X returns 0 (or last command's rc, often 0)
                  # rc captured as 0
                  returns 0

    Bash propagates errexit-suppression from a parent '||'/'if'/'!'
    into every shell function called from that context, and the
    suppression sticks across recursion. 'make_parse_cmd' (called via
    'make_function_run make_parse_cmd "$@"') is therefore unable to
    propagate failures from the per-target 'make_function_run
    "$target_fn"' it dispatches; the rc gets dropped on the floor and
    the script falls through to a clean exit 0.

    Fix: have 'make_function_run' 'exit' (not 'return') on failure.
    'exit' bypasses errexit-suppression unconditionally and ends the
    script with the inner command's exit code.

    The one caller that intentionally catches a failure ('if !
    make_function_run sq_git_run "HEAD"' in make_git_commit_verify,
    to attach a context-specific 'die' message) needs the called
    function to be able to return non-zero without exiting. Move that
    caller -- and sq_git_run itself -- off the make_function_run
    wrapper so the 'if !' branch can fire. Hooks for an external
    binary like 'sq-git' (function name with a dash) wouldn't have
    fired in practice anyway.

    Verified end-to-end with mocked sq-git: failure paths now propagate
    the inner rc (1, 42, etc.); success paths still exit 0; the custom
    "head commit is unsigned" die-message in make_git_commit_verify
    still prints.

