commit f38fba7a6858cb9aded2aa08cc8574f5838ce85d
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun May 17 12:51:16 2026 +0000

    genmkfile: fix special-repo path past the make-helper.bsh preamble

    Two real bugs in PR #15's earlier landing surfaced once `genmkfile
    git-tag-show` was actually exercised on a special repo (no
    debian/control, override file in place):

    1. shared.bsh's make_shared_function is called by make-helper.bsh:56
       BEFORE override files get sourced (make-helper.bsh needs
       dpkg_print_architecture for cross-arch defaults). At that point
       make_use_git_describe_for_version was unset, so the flag-gated
       branch fell through to the `test -f debian/control` failure -
       same die mode as before PR #15.

       Drop the flag-gated branch. Just probe debian/control directly:
       set both path variables to empty when the file is absent, don't
       die. Downstream consumers that genuinely need the file
       (make_get_dependencies grep-dctrl, make_get_variables
       dpkg-parsechangelog) already handle empty paths or die with a
       clear message. The flag itself remains in scope for
       make_get_variables, which is what actually picks the
       version-source strategy.

    2. make_get_variables' special-repo branch did not set
       make_source_package_name. make_git_tag_shared (line 1784) reads
       it under errexit/nounset just to compare with "derivative-maker",
       so any tag-related target hit `unbound variable`. Set it to the
       repo's directory basename ("qubes-template-kicksecure" etc.),
       matching the convention genmkfile already uses elsewhere. Also
       set make_package_list to a one-element array of the same name,
       for symmetry with the regular branch.

    Verified end-to-end:
    - genmkfile git-tag-show on qubes-template-kicksecure with an
      annotated tag at HEAD now prints "commit_<sha>".
    - Without any tag, dies with the helpful
      "no git tag reachable from HEAD; sign one with
      dm-quickgittagsign first" message added in PR #15.
    - Regular packages with debian/control: unchanged behavior.

