commit ce24570986cc378d30295ad16bcfd7c600b07b55
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun May 17 11:26:57 2026 +0000

    make_git_tag_sign: dispatch on make_use_git_describe_for_version

    Special repos opted in via make_use_git_describe_for_version (qubes
    templates, Whonix-Installer, Whonix-Starter) previously had to be
    tagged via a separate dm-quickgittagsign call in
    dm-packaging-helper-script's pkg_git_sign_tags, because the genmkfile
    make_git_tag_sign would attempt to create a tag named after
    make_git_tag_version_number = `git describe --abbrev=0` (the existing
    nearest tag) and fail.

    Move the polymorphism here: when make_use_git_describe_for_version is
    set, make_git_tag_sign overrides make_git_tag_version_number to
    commit_<HEAD-sha> and short-circuits if such a tag already exists at
    HEAD. Same SHA-encoded scheme dm-quickgittagsign(1) uses, so the two
    producers stay consistent; the prefix is `commit_` (was `adrelanos_`
    in the standalone script).

    Callers can now invoke `genmkfile git-tag-sign` uniformly for both
    kinds of repo; no in-caller dispatch needed.

