commit a087d92bd9095866a3717d5bb45d75b7c147a920
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue May 12 17:46:02 2026 +0000

    scorecard: remove consumer-scorecard.yml (org-wide opt-out)

    Per the consumer-template architecture's opt-in-by-file-presence
    rule, deleting a consumer-*.yml is the opt-out signal:
    pkg_update_consumer_workflows refreshes only files that already
    exist on the consumer side; the next propagation pass will not
    re-create this.

    Org-wide policy: Scorecard's value-to-noise ratio is low (many
    false positives, non-actionable signals). Keeping it only in
    derivative-maker (the canonical baseline) where the org-wide
    supply-chain signal is most useful.

    Spec:
    https://github.com/org-ai-assisted/developer-meta-files/blob/master/agents/github-actions-consumer-templates.md

