commit 152849b2bfc41308dcc8ded2b808c9120fab962b
Author: claude-code <claude-code@assisted-by-ai>
Date:   Wed May 6 13:26:30 2026 +0000

    fix(deb-{build,all}-dep): hardcode dctrl-tools alongside build-essential

    dctrl-tools (provides grep-dctrl) is added to the install lists of
    make_deb_build_dep and make_deb_all_dep alongside the existing
    build-essential. genmkfile cannot truly self-bootstrap dctrl-tools
    because make_get_dependencies needs grep-dctrl to parse
    debian/control in the first place - so the first ever run on a
    clean image without dctrl-tools still has to be primed manually
    (apt install dctrl-tools, or apt-get build-dep .).

    Once primed, this hardcoded include keeps it explicit:
    - on a re-run, dctrl-tools stays installed.
    - on a fresh checkout where build-essential is being installed
      anyway by these targets, dctrl-tools rides along in the same
      apt-get call rather than being a hidden runtime requirement.

    Note: debian/control already declares dctrl-tools in Build-Depends;
    this hardcoding is genmkfile's own apt-install path saying 'I need
    this tool myself' rather than relying on the package-build machinery
    to read debian/control.

